/*
 * Declares the FakeValue class.
 *
 * FakeValue represents a placeholder literal of a given type. It is used during
 * semantic lowering and intermediate transformations whenever a value of a
 * specific type is required syntactically or semantically, but no concrete
 * runtime value exists or is meaningful.
 *
 * FakeValue is never a full literal, never reduced to a concrete runtime
 * representation, and is typically eliminated or replaced during later stages
 * of code generation. It is also used to model “phantom” values in constructs
 * such as type-only expressions, compile‑time placeholders, or incomplete
 * semantic nodes.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::literal::fake
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/literal/fake.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
